      "content": "I'll start by orienting: what state is the board in, and what changed in the repository since my last shift?Board state noted: the three human-action cards (`b776e9a7`, `a8be6182`, `82314f38`) are still open, and the 12:00Z watchdog (`3cb512b4`) is 47 minutes from firing. Two agents ran this morning (software_developer 10:58, qa 11:09) \u2014 I need to know whether they touched the docs tree before the freeze.The docs set has **grown** since my last measurement: 7 entries \u2192 9 authored files, plus two untracked pages. `features/ciso.md` is brand new and appears to have no owner. Let me verify what these files are and whether they are in the published build.Two material findings already: `features/ciso.md` is a **brand-new, unowned page already wired into the public nav** (`config.mts` + `features/index.md` + `users-and-security.md`), and **51 files (+25,851 lines) of `.codx` control-plane state are staged in the git index**. Let me check the new page's claims and whether the untracked strategy doc can reach the build.The staged set is **7 docs files (+374)** \u2014 but the working tree has **5 more authored changes** the same VitePress build would publish. That distinction matters: a build reads the working tree, not the git index. Let me confirm the build config and what the untracked strategy file actually is.Evidence is conclusive. Three facts change the decision picture materially, all measured at 11:13Z:\n\n1. **7 of the docs files are already staged** in the git index (+374) \u2014 the approval is one `git commit` from `main`, not a review step.\n2. **The same index holds 44 `.codx` files (+25,477 lines)** \u2014 so a commit meant to publish 7 docs files would also publish agent bookkeeping.\n3. **`config.mts` has no `srcExclude`** \u2014 the VitePress build reads the *working tree*, so `features/ciso.md` (168 lines, unowned) and `transformation/ai-company.md` (3,215 lines of internal strategy) are published by the next build regardless of approval state.\n\nRecording this on the cards that are about to be acted on.Now the two cards that govern the index itself \u2014 and I've found the command on `82314f38` is incomplete: without a `.gitignore` entry, the next agent shift re-stages the same 42 files.One page in the tree has no owning card at all \u2014 `features/ciso.md`. Before assigning it, let me check the available profiles rather than guess.Card `721dc223` already contains better provenance evidence than I had when I wrote my comment \u2014 it establishes there is **no deploy target in this repository** (`docs:dev` only, no `dist/`, `fetch_webpage` \u2192 404). My wording overstated \"publishable\". Correcting myself before the report.Profiles confirmed: `biblio` (page/resource verdicts), `wiki` (codx-junior public docs), `web_master` (web content), `software_developer` (config changes). Creating the one card that is genuinely missing \u2014 `features/ciso.md` has no owner anywhere \u2014 with `biblio` owning it, since the deliverable is a verdict plus correction, not a code change.\n\n---\n\n> \u23f8 **Turn paused by the effort budget** \u2014 Maximum tool rounds (10) exceeded. The model keeps requesting tools without producing a final answer.\n>\n> This task ran as a **plain chat** (10 model rounds, no continuation). Add the `codx-junior` profile for the agile tier, or `codx-junior-max` for the max tier, to the task's profiles \u2014 or mention `@codx-junior-max` in your message. The round limit comes from the profile's `effort` block; raise `effort.max_iterations` there if it is not enough.\n\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\uddf0 Tool usage summary\n\n# Shift summary \u2014 19 Nov 2026, 11:13Z (shift 8, ProjectManager)\n\n## Useful findings (do not re-measure)\n\n- **Staged index:** `project_changes(scope=\"staged\")` = **51 files, +25,851/\u221252**; filtered to docs paths = **7 files, +374/\u22120** (`config.mts` +2, `browser-use.md` +91, `chats-and-agents.md` +4, `index.md` +2, `suggested-replies.md` +88 new, `users-and-security.md` +2, `voice-conversation.md` +185 new).\n- **Working tree (published by next build):** `scope=\"all\"` on docs paths = **10 files, +424/\u22120**; extra vs staged: `features/code-review.md` +40, untracked `features/ciso.md` (**168 lines**) and untracked `transformation/ai-company.md` (**3,215 lines**).\n- **Build config:** `.vitepress/config.mts` line 10 `ignoreDeadLinks: true`; **no `srcExclude`** \u2192 every `.md` compiles. Nav adds Suggested replies, Voice conversation, CISO.\n- **`features/ciso.md`** (read, 168 lines): claims a deterministic engine, \u201cNo security decision is delegated to an LLM.\u201d\n- **`transformation/ai-company.md`**: `Status: Proposal \u2014 for review and decision`; audience names \u201cthe first pilot companies\u201d.\n- **Cards:** `3cb512b4` (escalation watchdog",
      "think": "* Processing request, please wait...\n",
      "reasoning_content": "Let me get a focused view. Key facts from the diff: 68 files, +40095/-438 vs HEAD. That's the .codx bookkeeping noise (tasks). Which is exactly M6's problem.\n\nWhat's the situation? Previous shift report says pending docs approval set: 7 entries, +101/-0. Deadline 12:00Z today for escalation watchdog 3cb512b4.\n\nNow it's 11:13Z. The 12:00Z watchdog fires in ~47 min. And there's a task 68566d25 (biblio verdict before 12:00Z freeze) with wake_at 12:30. And 07006e18 (P0 design reviews published on public docs site) wake_at 12:30.\n\nMy agenda: nothing due. So I should decide from boards.\n\nKey thing to check: did anything change in the docs tree overnight? Let me measure the docs-only diff (excluding .codx) to check whether the approval set is still 7 entries. Note: two new shift files: qa shift at 11:09, software_developer shift at 10:58, ciso at 08:52. Those agents ran this morning.\n\nLet me measure:\n1. project_changes with paths filter for docs content (excluding .codx).\n2. Check whether the 12:00 watchdog's condition is still met \u2014 the approval and decision are still unanswered (b776e9a7 onhold, a8be6182 onhold). Yes, agenda shows both still onhold / User action needed.\n\nSo the watchdog will fire at 12:00 and must write the off-track report. That's a task scheduled at 12:00 with wake_at 12:00 \u2014 it will wake an agent. Actually wait \u2014 wake_at on a task triggers autonomy worker. Fine.\n\nWhat is genuinely useful for this shift (11:13Z, 47 min before the deadline)?\n\nOptions:\na) Pre-empt the 12:00 watchdog so the consequence is real, not just a card: e.g., verify that the freeze is well-defined, that the watchdog has everything it needs (list of 7 entries, the exact commit, the exact ratify/revert commands). Since no human answered in 3 days, the most valuable PM action is to make the decision cost lower and the consequence concrete.\nb) Measure the docs diff again to see if it grew (the qa and software_developer age