ce: 44 .codx files staged as A (added vs HEAD), meaning they're NOT in HEAD... wait \"A added\" vs HEAD means new to the index relative to HEAD. Earlier the diff vs HEAD showed them as A added \u2014 so .codx files are newly added to the index, i.e. previously untracked. So they are NOT yet tracked in HEAD! That changes the framing: `git rm -r --cached` is the wrong command \u2014 the correct one is simply `git restore --staged .codx` / `git rm --cached -r .codx` (equivalent for newly added), because they were untracked and someone staged them.\n\nThat's an important correction: card title says \"Run `git rm -r --cached` for .codx runtime state\". If .codx was never committed, then they're staged additions \u2014 unstage, don't remove from tracking. And crucially: **were any .codx files already in HEAD?** The diff showed `.codx/autonomy/state.json` and `.codx/harness/audit.jsonl` as `M modified` \u2014 those ARE tracked in HEAD. So .codx IS partially tracked: two files tracked (modified), and ~42 task JSONs newly added.\n\nSo the accurate command set:\n- Unstage the newly added task state: `git restore --staged '.codx'` (keeps files on disk, untracked)\n- For the two already-tracked files: `.codx/autonomy/state.json`, `.codx/harness/audit.jsonl` \u2192 these need `git rm --cached` to stop tracking (that's the real \"stop versioning\" step).\n- Then add `.codx` to .gitignore.\n\nLet me verify counts: staged 51 = 7 docs + 44 .codx. Of the 44: 2 modified (tracked) + 42 added (new). I'll state approx: \"2 modified tracked files + the rest newly added\".\n\nPrecisely from the earlier full listing: M .codx/autonomy/state.json, M .codx/harness/audit.jsonl, A .codx/tasks/.archive/... , A index.json, A several shift jsons... yes 2 M + 42 A.\n\nGood \u2014 that's a genuinely useful correction and it changes the human's 5-minute job: currently the card says `git rm -r --cached` which on tracked files is right, but it would leave the 42 staged additions untouched if run only on