          "response": "{\n  \"count\": 23,\n  \"total\": 23,\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6c697929-d89c-4a92-87c0-251fcd27d47b\",\n      \"name\": \"QA gate can return `allow` with the tests switched off (`run_tests=False`), and its `paths` filter is defeated by `.codx` \\u2014 a false green is reachable\",\n      \"status\": \"onhold\",\n      \"mode\": \"chat\",\n      \"board\": \"IT team\",\n      \"column\": \"Scheduled\",\n      \"sprints\": [\n        \"QA gate hardening (18-21 Nov 2026)\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": \"high\",\n      \"due_date\": \"2026-11-20\",\n      \"wake_at\": \"2026-11-20T09:00:00+00:00\",\n      \"schedule\": null,\n      \"schedule_context\": \"history\",\n      \"progress\": 0,\n      \"assignees\": [\n        \"software_developer\"\n      ],\n      \"profiles\": [\n        \"software_developer\"\n      ],\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"qa-gate\",\n        \"false-positive\",\n        \"tooling\"\n      ],\n      \"parent_id\": \"30d9441e-2718-425e-9909-b1e8c54a4ec1\",\n      \"project_id\": \"3921fcc6-1860-4daf-8689-c3fd77f2cc40\",\n      \"owner_project_id\": \"3921fcc6-1860-4daf-8689-c3fd77f2cc40\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-11-18 11:25:39.893472\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-11-19T11:12:27.092434\",\n      \"description\": \"## Context\\n\\nMeasured by QA on 2026-11-18 while correcting a wrong figure on card `17efa3eb` (M5). The QA gate can currently produce a green verdict **without verifying anything**, and its per-path counts are dominated by `.codx` control-plane noise.\\n\\nThis is separate from `3fb379ae` (\\\"no test suite declared\\\"). That card fixes the *absence* of a suite; this card fixes the *reporting* that makes the absence invisible.\\n\\n## Measured evidence (same tree, same shift)\\n\\n| call | result |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `qa_review_changes(scope=\\\"all\\\", paths=[\\\"qa\\\",\\\"features\\\"], run_tests=False)` | `decision: allow`, `findings: 0`, `highest_severity: none` |\\n| `qa_review_changes(scope=\\\"all\\\", paths=[\\\"qa\\\",\\\"features\\\"], run_tests=True)` | `decision: block`, `[high] tests.no-suite` |\\n| `qa_plan(paths=[\\\".codx\\\"])` | `changed_files: 32` |\\n| `qa_plan(paths=[\\\"qa\\\",\\\"features\\\"])` | `changed_files: 1` |\\n| `qa_plan(paths=[\\\"delivery-contract.md\\\", \\\".vitepress\\\"])` | `changed_files: 0` |\\n| `project_changes(scope=\\\"all\\\", paths=[\\\"delivery-contract.md\\\"])` | 1 file modified, **+44/\\u221213** |\\n\\n## What must change\\n\\n1. **`allow` must not be producible when the tests were not run.** Either refuse `run_tests=False` verdicts, or label the result explicitly (e.g. `verdict: not_verified` / `tests_executed: false`) so it cannot be quoted as \\\"QA passed\\\".\\n2. **`qa_plan` must exclude `.codx` from `changed_files`**, or state in its output that the control plane is included. A path-scoped count that is 32/33 agent noise files is worse than no count.\\n3. **`qa_plan` and `project_changes` must agree** on the changed-file count for the same path. Today `delivery-contract.md` is modified per git and invisible (0) to `qa_plan`.\\n4. **`qa_policy` should be writable** by the owner of the gate configuration (`qa_policy` currently accepts only `action=\\\"show\\\"`, which is why `3fb379ae` cannot be closed from the QA side).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- `qa_review_changes(scope=\\\"all\\\", paths=[\\\"qa\\\",\\\"features\\\"], run_tests=False)` returns either a non-green verdict or an explicit `tests_executed: false` marker.\\n- `qa_plan(paths=[\\\".codx\\\"])` returns a `changed_files` count that excludes the control plane, or documents why it includes it.\\n- `qa_plan(paths=[\\\"delivery-contract.md\\\"])` and `project_changes(scope=\\\"all\\\", paths=[\\\"delivery-contract.md\\\"])` report the same file count.\\n- `qa_policy(action=\\\"set\\\", changes={...})` accepts a valid suite declaration (validated, not silently dropped).\\n\\n## Why it blocks the sprint demo\\n\\n`f6d1855e` (sprint review & demo, 2026-11-21) will quote QA verdicts. A `allow` obtained with `run_tests=False` is reachable today and would be presented as a pass. That is the exact failure this gate exists to prevent.\\n\\nOwner: `software_developer`. QA does not patch the gate it is measured ",
