o register **MCP servers** in their settings.\n \n+## Suggested replies\n+\n+When the AI needs a decision it can offer the likely answers as buttons at the end of its message. Clicking a button sends that answer as the next user message; the composer stays available, so the user can always write something different. See [Suggested replies](/features/suggested-replies) for the protocol and the options available to models.\n+\n The agent loop has guards against runaway behaviour: a maximum number of iterations (**Global settings \u2192 Agents**), a maximum number of tool calls per provider, loop detection, and a cancel button that stops the request at once. Every call is checked against the user's [budget](/features/budget-and-analytics) before it is sent.\n \n ## Working with messages\n```\n\n**`features/index.md`**\n```diff\ndiff --git a/features/index.md b/features/index.md\nindex b6c08eb..d3f3def 100755\n--- a/features/index.md\n+++ b/features/index.md\n@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@ context and stay in budget. This section documents every feature in detail.\n | Feature | Summary |\n | --- | --- |\n | [Chats and agents](/features/chats-and-agents) | Project-aware chats with modes, sub-chats, attachments and a tool-using agent loop. |\n+| [Suggested replies](/features/suggested-replies) | The model offers its likely answers as buttons; the user clicks one or writes their own. |\n+| [Voice conversation](/features/voice-conversation) | Call codx-junior: speak instructions, hear the answers, and keep every turn in the chat. |\n | [Kanban and tasks](/features/kanban) | Boards and columns where every card is a chat with sub-tasks, checklists and assignees. |\n | [Profiles](/features/profiles) | Reusable instructions that set the model, tools and coding standards. |\n | [Autonomous agents](/features/autonomous-agents) | Actors: profiles with initiative that take their own shifts, schedule their own follow-ups and work only inside a weekly availability window. |\n@@ -39,6 +41,7 @@ context and stay in budget. This section documents every feature in detail.\n | Feature | Summary |\n | --- | --- |\n | [G",
