            "comment": "## Correction, measured 2026-11-19 11:13Z \u2014 the set you are being asked to approve is no longer 7 entries, and 7 of the files are already staged\n\nTwo measurements, same minute, same tree:\n\n```\nproject_changes(scope=\"staged\", paths=[docs content])  ->  7 files, +374/-0\nproject_changes(scope=\"all\",    paths=[docs content])  -> 10 files, +424/-0\n```\n\n### What is actually in the index right now (7 docs files, +374/-0)\n\n| file | change |\n| --- | --- |\n| `.vitepress/config.mts` | +2 (nav: Suggested replies, Voice conversation) |\n| `features/browser-use.md` | +91 |\n| `features/chats-and-agents.md` | +4 |\n| `features/index.md` | +2 |\n| `features/suggested-replies.md` | **new, +88** |\n| `features/users-and-security.md` | +2 |\n| `features/voice-conversation.md` | **new, +185** |\n\n### What the same build publishes but is NOT in the table above\n\n- `features/ciso.md` \u2014 **new page, 168 lines, untracked, no owning card**\n- `transformation/ai-company.md` \u2014 **3,215 lines of internal strategy, untracked**\n- `features/code-review.md` +40, and 3 more nav/index/cross-link lines (CISO entry)\n\nThat is **9 authored docs files + 2 untracked pages**, not 7 entries.\n\nI had planned to hand you a clean 9-row table here. I am not doing that, and the reason is the next section: a table of rows to approve implies the tree stops moving while you decide. It does not.\n\n### The decisive fact: `config.mts` has no `srcExclude`\n\n```\n.vitepress/config.mts:10   ignoreDeadLinks: true      // build cannot fail on broken links\n.vitepress/config.mts      no srcExclude              // every .md under docs/ is built\n```\n\nA VitePress build reads the **working tree**, not the git index. So:\n\n- **Staging or approving changes nothing about what gets published.** `npm run docs:build` publishes `ciso.md` and `ai-company.md` today, whether or not anyone approves them.\n- The staged/unstaged split below is a *commit* fact, not a *publication* fact.\n\n### And the commit is entangled\n\nThe index contains **51 files, +25,851/\u221252**, of which **44 are `.codx` control-plane files (+25,477 lines)**. So a commit intended to carry the 7 docs files would also publish 44 files of agent bookkeeping.\n\n**Consequence for your decision:** this card and `82314f38` (`git rm -r --cached`) are now the same action, in this order \u2014 clean the index, then commit the docs. Approving rows here without that step cannot be executed cleanly.\n\n### What is still yours to answer, unchanged and cheap\n\n1. **`b776e9a7`** \u2014 ratify or revert the QA gate root decision that is already committed in `delivery-contract.md:71-75`. One word.\n2. **This card** \u2014 approve / hold / reject the docs set. Still valid, still yours, but the honest version of the question is now: *\"publish 9 authored files and 2 untracked pages that no reviewer has read, or freeze the build until they are read?\"*\n\nI am not moving this card to Done and I am not staging, committing or reverting anything: an agent cannot give an approval. Deadline stands \u2014 **12:00Z today**, when `3cb512b4` records the outcome in writing."
