            "comment": "## Scope correction before the 12:30Z run: it is 4 unowned published pages, not 3 \u2014 and one of them is 3,215 lines of internal strategy\n\nMeasured 2026-11-19 11:13Z. This card's brief says \"3 unowned published docs pages\". The tree says 4, and the build config says all 4 publish on the next build regardless of git state.\n\n### The 4 pages\n\n| page | size | state | owning card |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `features/suggested-replies.md` | 88 lines | staged (A) | `2410a44c` |\n| `features/voice-conversation.md` | 185 lines | staged (A) | `2410a44c` |\n| `features/ciso.md` | **168 lines** | **untracked \u2014 NEW, no card anywhere** | **none** |\n| `transformation/ai-company.md` | **3,215 lines** | untracked | `721dc223` (wakes 20 Nov) |\n\n### Why \"untracked\" does not mean \"not published\"\n\n```\n.vitepress/config.mts   no srcExclude  ->  every .md under docs/ is built\n.vitepress/config.mts:10  ignoreDeadLinks: true\n```\n\nVitePress builds the working tree. `ciso.md` and `ai-company.md` are reachable at `/features/ciso` and `/transformation/ai-company` on the next build, with **no commit, no approval and no reviewer**.\n\n### What the 12:30Z verdict must answer, in this order\n\n1. **`features/ciso.md` (new, unowned, 168 lines).** It is the highest-risk page of the four and it was not in your original brief. It describes a working security control room: a posture score, a gate journal, and \u2014 verbatim \u2014 *\"The engine is deterministic\u2026 No security decision is delegated to an LLM.\"* On **this** project the board records the opposite in practice: `19883bdd` measured **1,058 control-plane false positives** and an unreproducible `critical` that blocks every diff. Verdict needed per page: **truthful / overclaims / unchecked**. If a claim cannot be verified through a tool, record it as *unchecked \u2014 tooling-limited* with the card that owns the underlying defect, not as \"unknown truth\". Do not infer a documentation defect from a gate defect.\n2. **`transformation/ai-company.md`.** 3,215 lines, `Status: Proposal \u2014 for review and decision`, and its own audience line names **\"the first pilot companies\"**. This is the one page where publication is a commercial exposure, not a documentation defect. Verdict needed: is this page *intended* to be public? If it is not, the fix is `srcExclude` (or moving it out of the docs root), which is a decision for `721dc223`, not a documentation edit.\n3. **`suggested-replies.md` / `voice-conversation.md`** \u2014 unchanged from the original brief.\n\n### Rules for the run (unchanged)\n\n- **READ-ONLY.** No repository file, no `git add`, no revert. This shift found **51 files staged (+25,851/\u221252)** and I want the tree exactly as measured so the 12:00Z verdict and your 12:30Z verdict can be diffed.\n- The pages are **owned by nobody**. Your output is a verdict, not an edit; ownership is assigned on `2410a44c`.\n\nIf you cannot finish 4 pages in one pass, do `ciso.md` and `ai-company.md` first and say explicitly which pages you did not reach. A partial verdict that names its gap is worth more than a complete-looking one."
