            "comment": "## Pre-run amendment, 11:13Z \u2014 the baseline numbers for the 12:00Z verdict, and the freeze must cover the **build**, not the commit\n\nYou run in ~45 minutes. Two things in the original brief are now out of date, so here is the baseline measured at **11:13Z** to diff against, plus one correction to what \"freeze\" means.\n\n### Baseline to compare at 12:00Z (do not re-derive, just diff)\n\n```\nproject_changes(scope=\"staged\")                        -> 51 files, +25,851/-52\n  of which  docs:                                      7 files,  +374/-0\n  of which  .codx control plane:                      44 files, +25,477\nproject_changes(scope=\"all\", paths=[docs content])     -> 10 files, +424/-0\nuntracked, will be built:  features/ciso.md (168 lines), transformation/ai-company.md (3,215 lines)\n```\n\n### Status of the two blocking human actions at 11:13Z\n\n- `a8be6182` \u2014 **not answered.** No human approve/hold/reject; still `User action needed`, progress 0.\n- `b776e9a7` \u2014 **not answered.** Still `User action needed`, progress 0. The self-certified decision remains committed at `delivery-contract.md:71-75`.\n\nIf neither moved by 12:00, the verdict is **\"either unanswered\"** \u2192 sprint **off track**, as this card's brief already specifies. Do not soften it because \"something might arrive\": an unanswered deadline that is quietly extended is the exact failure this card exists to prevent.\n\n### The correction: freeze the build, not the commit\n\n`.vitepress/config.mts` has **no `srcExclude`** and sets `ignoreDeadLinks: true`. VitePress builds the **working tree**, not the index. So a \"freeze on the diff\" that only forbids `git commit` **does not freeze publication**:\n\n- `npm run docs:build` / any deploy publishes `features/ciso.md` (168 lines, unowned, unreviewed) and `transformation/ai-company.md` (3,215 lines of internal strategy whose audience line names *the first pilot companies*) \u2014 with no commit and no approval.\n\n**Therefore the 12:00Z outcome must state:** no docs build and no deploy until the diff is decided, and \u2014 if a build is unavoidable \u2014 `srcExclude` must carry `ciso.md` and `transformation/` first, as a one-line change on `721dc223`.\n\n### Report format for the 12:00Z post (keep it to one screen)\n\n1. **Verdict:** on track / off track \u2014 one word, first line.\n2. **Answered / not answered** per card, one line each.\n3. **Diff size at 12:00Z** vs the baseline above, and whether `browser-use.md` (+91) or `voice-conversation.md` (+185) moved again.\n4. **The unpaid human action**, named, with the commercial consequence: unreviewed customer-facing documentation is publishable on the next build, and no QA gate can run because the suite declaration (`e684ce5c`) and the gate root (`b776e9a7`) are both undecided.\n5. **Next step with a date** \u2014 not \"await approval\". Recommend the default if silence continues.\n\n### Still binding\n\nRead-only. No repository write, no staging, no revert, and **do not move `a8be6182` or `b776e9a7` to Done** \u2014 an agent cannot accept a human decision. Comment on `f6d1855e` (sprint demo, 21 Nov) and close this card once the verdict is written."
