            "chat_id": "2410a44c-186f-4bb6-ae86-49880c71d484",
            "comment": "## Intake update, 11:13Z \u2014 the unowned set is now 5 pages, and one of them I have to flag as the most exposed\n\nThis card's title says \"four unowned files\". A fifth arrived unannounced and it is the one I would act on first.\n\n### Current unowned authored set\n\n| page / file | size | state | note |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `features/ciso.md` | **168 lines** | **untracked, NEW, no card** | **new since yesterday 16:05Z** |\n| `transformation/ai-company.md` | **3,215 lines** | untracked | internal strategy; own audience = \"first pilot companies\"; decision card `721dc223` |\n| `features/voice-conversation.md` | 185 lines | staged (A) | |\n| `features/suggested-replies.md` | 88 lines | staged (A) | |\n| `features/browser-use.md` | +91 | staged (M) | modification, not new |\n| `features/code-review.md` | +40 | unstaged (M) | modification, not new |\n\n### The one that changes priority\n\n`features/ciso.md` is not just an unowned page \u2014 it is **already cross-linked into the published navigation in the working tree**:\n\n- `.vitepress/config.mts`: `{ text: 'CISO (security view)', link: '/features/ciso' }` (+1, unstaged)\n- `features/index.md`: CISO row in the feature table (+1, unstaged)\n- `features/users-and-security.md`: new \"Security posture\" section linking to it (+8, unstaged)\n\nSo a reader of the published site gets a nav entry, a table row, and a cross-link, all pointing at a page no reviewer has read. That is the same failure mode this card was opened to prevent, one level worse: the page and its three entry points arrived together and the entry points are what make it discoverable.\n\n### What I want from the intake work\n\n1. **Assign an owner to `ciso.md`** \u2014 put it on `68566d25` (biblio verdict, wakes **12:30 today**) rather than queueing it behind this card, because that run is the one that reads pages before the build.\n2. **Do not fold `ai-company.md` into a documentation fix.** Its publication question is a scope decision (`721dc223`), not an edit; the answer is likely `srcExclude`, not rewriting 3,215 lines.\n3. **Record the entry points, not only the pages.** For each new page, list the nav/index/cross-link lines that make it reachable. A page nobody can find is a smaller problem than three links pointing at it.\n4. **Keep the accounting split between staged and unstaged.** `project_changes(scope=\"staged\")` = 7 docs files / +374; the working tree = 10 authored files / +424. Reporting one number invites the reader to assume the build follows the index. It does not.\n\n### Unchanged constraints\n\nRead-only with respect to the working tree \u2014 no staging, no revert, no new docs content. This card is intake and ownership, not authoring. If the intake now implies authoring work, that is a new card with a named `biblio` owner, not an extension of this one."
          },
          "response": "{\n  \"status\": \"comment_added\",\n  \"task_id\": \"2410a44c-186f-4bb6-ae86-49880c71d484\",\n  \"message_id\": null,\n  \"processed\": false\n}",
          "output": "\ud83d\udcdd Comment added to task **Intake \u2014 four unowned files sit in the working tree management approves tomorrow (voice-conversation docs page + attribution spec + 2 nav lines)**.\n- ID: `2410a44c-186f-4bb6-ae86-49880c71d484`\n- No processing was triggered: the request waits for a user.",
