        {
          "tool": "project_manager",
          "tool_call_id": "call_00_3LtdgowLchoOVXsxhzof4817",
          "status": "done",
          "request": {
            "action": "request_help",
            "chat_id": "82314f38-2433-43f5-aec6-91b6544ce65b",
            "comment": "## 11:13Z \u2014 the command on this card is correct but **incomplete**, and it now has an ordering constraint against the docs approval\n\nMeasured now: the index holds **51 files, +25,851/\u221252**. Breakdown:\n\n| bucket | files | lines |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `.codx` control plane | **44** | **+25,477** |\n| authored docs | 7 | +374 |\n\nOf the 44 `.codx` files, **2 are already tracked and modified** (`.codx/autonomy/state.json` +92/\u221252, `.codx/harness/audit.jsonl` +819) and **42 are newly staged additions** (task JSONs, `.codx/tasks/.archive/`, agent shift records).\n\n### Two corrections to this card\n\n**1. The missing half of the fix: `.gitignore`.**\n\n42 `.codx` files are *staged additions*, which proves `.codx` is not ignored. So `git rm -r --cached .codx` alone fixes today's index and **guarantees the same 44 files are back tomorrow** \u2014 the agents write them every shift, and nothing stops them being staged again. The fix is two steps, and the second one is the one that holds:\n\n```\ngit rm -r --cached .codx          # today's index\nprintf '\\n.codx/\\n' >> .gitignore # every future shift\n```\n\nWithout the second line this card is a recurring chore, not a fix. That is also why `8909f356` (M6) exists \u2014 this card is its immediate, manual half.\n\n**2. Ordering: this must run *before* the docs commit, and the two are now one action.**\n\nA `git commit` in this repository today would publish the 7 docs files **and** 44 files of agent bookkeeping in the same object. So whoever approves on `a8be6182` cannot execute that approval cleanly until this card runs.\n\n**Recommended sequence (5\u201310 minutes, one shell):**\n\n1. `git rm -r --cached .codx` + the `.gitignore` line\n2. commit the 7 docs files on their own \u2014 the diff an approver is actually reviewing\n3. `a8be6182` becomes executable as a normal docs commit\n\n### Safety note, since the tree is not clean\n\nNothing here is destructive: `--cached` leaves every file on disk. But the repository now has **three** distinct states \u2014 index (51), working tree authored content (10), and untracked pages not in either (`ciso.md`, `transformation/ai-company.md`). If someone runs `git stash` or `git checkout .` to \"clean up\" before committing, the unowned pages are the ones at risk. Take a branch or nothing at all; do not stash.\n\nStill `User action needed` \u2014 no shell in the agent profiles, so I cannot run this. I am not moving the card: it stays open until someone reports the output of those two commands."
          },
          "response": "{\n  \"status\": \"comment_added\",\n  \"task_id\": \"82314f38-2433-43f5-aec6-91b6544ce65b\",\n  \"message_id\": null,\n  \"processed\": false\n}",
          "output": "\ud83d\udcdd Comment added to task **Run `git rm -r --cached` for .codx runtime state (needs a shell; agent profile has none)**.\n- ID: `82314f38-2433-43f5-aec6-91b6544ce65b`\n- No processing was triggered: the request waits for a user.",
