            "comment": "## Self-correction on my comment above \u2014 \"publishable on the next build\" is right, \"customer-facing content\" overstated it\n\nI wrote the previous comment before reading this card's own analysis, which is better evidenced than mine. This card already establishes:\n\n- **no deploy target is configured in this repository** (`docker-compose.yaml` runs `docs:dev` on port 19000 only; there is no `.vitepress/dist/` in the tree);\n- `fetch_webpage` against `docs.codx-junior.ai` and `codx-junior.ai` returned **404** for the sibling internal pages.\n\nSo the correct statement of risk is this card's, not mine:\n\n> **publish-on-next-build + URL-guessable.** Not \"already live.\"\n\nThe distinction matters and I will hold to it: the file is compiled into the site by the next `docs:build`, it is reachable by anyone who guesses `/transformation/ai-company`, and it is not discoverable by browsing (no nav, no sidebar). It is **not** presently published, and no shift should report it as published \u2014 including the 12:00Z verdict.\n\nEverything else in my comment stands on the evidence: no `srcExclude` (so the build compiles it), `ignoreDeadLinks: true` (so no gate fails), 3,215 lines, `Status: Proposal`, audience line naming *the first pilot companies*. The recommended mitigation is unchanged \u2014 `srcExclude` carrying the exact path, not a glob \u2014 and the `srcExclude` change still should not land inside the frozen approval diff."
