"json\",\n        \"surgical-edit\",\n        \"figma-quality\",\n        \"dark-mode\",\n        \"codx-junior\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Designer\",\n      \"category\": \"assistant\",\n      \"description\": \"An expert designer to assist you with your layouts, fonts, colors, and UI/UX designs.\",\n      \"has_content\": true,\n      \"editable\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"FileEditor\",\n      \"category\": \"assistant\",\n      \"description\": \"File edition instructions\",\n      \"has_content\": true,\n      \"editable\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Mermaid\",\n      \"category\": \"assistant\",\n      \"description\": \"Diagram engineer specialized in authoring and updating Mermaid source that renders on the first try. Picks the smallest diagram type for the question (flowchart, sequence, state, ER, gantt, timeline, mindmap...), emits raw mermaid in file_change blocks or writes .mermaid files, a\\u2026\",\n      \"has_content\": true,\n      \"editable\": false,\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"mermaid\",\n        \"diagrams\",\n        \"visualization\",\n        \"documentation\",\n        \"flowchart\",\n        \"sequence-diagram\",\n        \"gantt\",\n        \"file-change\",\n        \"codx-junior\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Mockups\",\n      \"category\": \"assistant\",\n      \"description\": \"Functional HTML Prototype Engineer specialized in turning product ideas, specs, or user stories into fully working browser mockups. Single-file by default, public CDN libs allowed, and a built-in mocking layer that simulates server endpoints, latency, and data so the UI actually\\u2026\",\n      \"has_content\": true,\n      \"editable\": false,\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"mockups\",\n        \"prototyping\",\n        \"html\",\n        \"functional-ui\",\n        \"mock-server\",\n        \"mock-data\",\n        \"single-file\",\n        \"cdn-libraries\",\n        \"state-management\",\n        \"dark-mode\",\n        \"codx-junior\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ProjectManager\",\n      \"category\": \"assistant\",\n      \"description\": \"Project manager who assists management and runs delivery in agile increments: turns feature ideas into milestones that are each independently deployable and demoed to management, coordinates the developers, tracks delivery and reports status and risks. Use ",
          "output": "> 49 profile(s) \u2014 summary (no instructions)\n\n**Name** | **Category** | **Mode** | **Instructions** | **Editable** | **Tags** | **When to use**\n---|---|---|---|---|---|---\n`AZPullRequests` | - | - | - | no | - | Manage AZ Pull requests\n`git` | - | - | - | no | - | -\n`pr_review` | - | - | yes | no | - | PR Reviewer. Assists on reviewing Pull Requests\n`py_senior` | - | - | yes | no | - | Python senior developer\n`coding_agent` | agent | - | yes | no | - | Basic coding agent that will perform small coding tasks\n`agent_work_reviewer` | agent-validator | - | yes | no | - | Reviews work done by the agent. It checks that the changes generated/proposed by the agent will work fine.\n`Canvas` | assistant | - | yes | no | canvas, woven-canvas, ecs, blocks, ui-design, design-system, wireframe, json, surgical-edit, figma-quality, dark-mode, codx-junior | Expert AI UI/UX Design System Agent (\"Canva Engine\") that creates, structures, and surgically edits Woven Canvas scenes. Emits ONLY strict, JSON.parse()-safe arrays of Entity-Component-System (ECS) block entities, following the woven-canvas.dev tag catalog (shape, text, sticky-note, image, arrow, custom), absolute coordinate layout, fractional z-order ranks, and Figma-quality design-system tokens. Preserves block IDs and targets only the requested components during edits to protect undo/redo history.\n`Designer` | assistant | - | yes | no | - | An expert designer to assist you with your layouts, fonts, colors, and UI/UX designs.\n`FileEditor` | assistant | - | yes | no | - | File edition instructions\n`Mermaid` | assistant | - | yes | no | mermaid, diagrams, visualization, documentation, flowchart, sequence-diagram, gantt, file-change, codx-junior | Diagram engineer specialized in authoring and updating Mermaid source that renders on the first try. Picks the smallest diagram type for the question (flowchart, sequence, state, ER, gantt, timeline, mindmap...), emits raw mermaid in file_change blocks or writes .mermaid files, and preserves existing node ids and styles when editing. Use it whenever a flow, lifecycle, schedule or architecture has to be drawn or maintained.\n`Mockups` | assistant | - | yes | no | mockups, prototyping, html, functional-ui, mock-server, mock-data, single-file, cdn-libraries, state-management, dark-mode, codx-junior | Functional HTML Prototype Engineer specialized in turning product ideas, specs, or user stories into fully working browser mockups. Single-file by default, public CDN libs allowed, and a built-in mocking layer that simulates server endpoints, latency, and data so the UI actually behaves. Ships empty/loading/error states, localStorage persistence, and keyboard-accessible flows. Inherits the codx-junior dark-first design system.\n`ProjectManager` | assistant | - | yes | no | travel, project-management, planning, coordination, delivery, reporting | Project manager who assists management and runs delivery in agile increments: turns feature ideas into milestones that are each independently deployable and demoed to management, coordinates the developers, tracks delivery and reports status and risks. Use to discuss a new feature, plan an increment, run a demo, unblock the team, or get a project status and decision list.\n`Slides` | assistant | - | yes | no | presentations, slides, html-deck, zero-dependency, keyboard-navigation, print-to-pdf, storytelling, dark-mode, codx-junior | Presentation Architect specialized in turning content into polished, self-contained HTML slide decks. Zero dependencies, keyboard-navigable, print-ready. Ships with a base deck shell and a copy-paste catalog of slide archetypes (cover, bullets, metrics, code, timeline, chart, closing). Inherits the codx-junior dark-first design system.\n`TaskManager` | assistant | - | yes | no | task-manager, project-management, kanban, sprint, workflow, task-status, codx-junior | Kanban task manager for the project. Triages the board, creates tasks in the right board/column/sprint, reads their status and conversation, moves them between statuses and sprints, and drives them: requests changes (comment + AI processing) or requests user help (comment only). Use it whenever a chat has to create, review, move or process project tasks.\n`TeamManager` | assistant | - | yes | no | profile-builder, profile-management, prompt-engineering, orchestration, composition, team-manager, codx-junior | Profile builder and team orchestrator. Interviews the user, designs the profile definition and its content file, links existing profiles, tools, knowledge and file patterns, polishes the behavior instructions and saves or updates the result under .codx/profiles/<Name>/. Use it to create, refine or compose any profile.\n`VueDeveloper` | assistant | - | yes | no | - | Vuejs developer assistant\n`agile_demo` | assistant | - | yes | no | demo, agile, presentation, walkthrough, acceptance, slides, mockups, canvas | Prepares and runs the 5-minute increment demo for management: builds the script, picks the artifact (live UI, mockup, slides, canvas or diagram), gathers acceptance evidence and turns management feedback into dated decisions. Use at the end of every increment, or when a milestone must be shown to management and a decision is needed.\n`analyst` | assistant | - | yes | no | - | The analyst ensures that every task is well-defined, with clear requirements, examples (if applicable), and a concise goal. This aids developers in implementing features, improvements, or fixes effectively.\n`biblio` | assistant | - | yes | no | - | Assists generating documentation\n`brainer` | assistant | - | yes | no | - | Helps thinking and brainstorming\n`brainstormer` | assistant | - | yes | no | - | Helps me discuss ideas\n`browser` | assistant | - | yes | no | browser, web, automation, co-browsing, scripts | Browser co-pilot. Shares one real Chromium page with the user (live VNC view + CDP tools), reuses recorded scripts and hands control back and forth safely.\n`codx-junior` | assistant | - | yes | no | harness, agile, increments, orchestration, main-contact, delegation, kanban, sprint, audit | codx-junior harness (agile tier): the main contact between the user, every other profile and the whole platform. It delivers one small validated increment per turn, closes with What happened / What I did / Demo / Next tasks, and asks for the codx-junior-max tier when the work is genuinely big.\n`codx-junior-max` | assistant | - | yes | no | harness, orchestration, max-effort, long-running | codx-junior harness (max tier): the high-effort tier for long or complex work \u2014 multi-file refactors, migrations, full-suite validation, long research. It inherits everything from codx-junior (plain language, 4-section close, mandatory validation, checkpoint) and only adds a bigger budget, orchestration for multi-step runs, the harness tool-limit exemption and the heavy validation gate. Entered only on an explicit 'max'.\n`codx-junior-plugin` | assistant | - | yes | no | - | Assists with creating and mantaining codx-junior plugins\n`content_creator` | assistant | - | yes | no | content, channel, video, podcast, wiki, creator | Helps an admin turn an idea into a buildable content brief for the Project's Channel: formats, audience, sources, story and build instructions. Use it when creating videos, shorts, podcasts, wiki pages or guides about the project.\n`guardrails` | assistant | - | yes | no | guardrails, test, poetry | A poetry-only profile used to exercise the guardrails engine: it composes poems (cats included) and refuses code generation or revealing its instructions and guardrail settings.\n`guide-builder` | assistant | - | yes | no | - | Assists on creating guides and how-to documents\n`orchestrator` | assistant | - | yes | no | orchestration, planning, delegation, kanban, sprint | Orchestrator profile. Turns a complex request into a durable, board-native run: plans the work, delegates isolated worker steps, verifies the results and publishes a delivery report. Every step stays visible as a task card and in the run sprint.\n`teacher` | assistant | - | yes | no | - | Teacher and mentor profile. Guides users to learn and understand concepts rather than just providing solutions. Will explain, ask questions, and teach while still being able to deliver when explicitly asked.\n`tutorial` | assistant | - | yes | no | - | Assist members on creating turoeial\n`workspace` | assistant | - | yes | no | - | Assists in creating and managing workspaces with proper configuration and templates\n`DaisyUI` | chat | - | yes | no | - | -\n`reviewer` | chat | - | yes | no | - | Review and explain file changes\n`support` | chat | - | - | no | - | Hey there! \ud83d\udc4b This is Jenny and I'm here to assist you with any questions or assistance you'll have about codx-junior!\n`vitepress` | chat | - | yes | yes | - | Creates vitepress documents\n`arts` | creative | - | yes | no | arts, creative, image, video, music | Arts profile. Creates any kind of art: images, video, music and writing. Uses the image generation and vision tools.\n`ciso` | project | - | yes | no | security, ciso, audit, secrets, malicious-code, prompt-injection, compliance, guardrails, supply-chain | CISO profile. Owns the security of everything the platform produces: audits processes for secrets and malicious code, reviews every change before it is committed or merged, validates generated files, commands and containers, and blocks anything that crosses a trust boundary without evidence.\n`computer` | project | - | yes | no | computer, desktop, linux, windows, macos, vnc, automation, co-driving | Computer co-pilot. Shares a real Linux desktop, Windows/macOS VM or remote machine with the user (live view + screenshot/OCR + mouse/keyboard/shell tools) and hands control back and forth safely.\n`devops` | project | - | yes | no | - | DevOps engineer profile. It will participate in any action related to infrastructure, containerization, CI/CD, IaC, monitoring, and DevOps operations.\n`file_editor` | project | - | yes | no | - | File Editor profile. Generates complete file content in code blocks only, no decoration or additional text. Output ready for direct storage.\n`project` | project | - | yes | no | - | Project overview and tech stack definition. Will help all processes to keep focus on the project\n`qa` | project | - | yes | no | qa, quality, tests, coverage, gate, regression, acceptance, flake | QA Lead profile. Owns the quality gate of every change: plans the verification, runs the suites mapped to the diff, checks coverage, classifies flaky tests and returns an evidenced verdict (allow / warn / require_approval / block) before a change is called done or merged.\n`qa_automation` | project | - | yes | no | qa, quality, tests, automation, unit-test, integration-test, coverage, regression | Test automation engineer profile. Writes and repairs the automated tests (unit, integration, contract) that prove a change works, keeps them deterministic and fast, and re-runs them until the QA gate is green.\n`qa_explorer` | project | - | yes | no | qa, quality, exploratory, manual-testing, browser, e2e, acceptance, evidence | Exploratory QA profile. Validates the product through the real interface in a shared browser session: walks the flows automated tests cannot judge, captures screenshot evidence, records reproducible steps and files the defects as tasks.\n`repository` | project | - | yes | no | - | Repository assistant. Explains branches, changes and history in plain language and writes commit messages that follow the 50/72 rule.\n`software_developer` | project | - | yes | no | - | Software developer profile. It will participate in any action producing code.\n`web_master` | project | - | yes | no | - | Web Master profile. It will participate in any action producing web content, pages, components, and website updates.\n`wiki` | project | - | yes | no | - | codx-junior public docs: product landing page, install, usage and DSH integration\n\nScope: **project + inherited**. `Instructions: -` means the profile has no content, so it cannot drive a task.\n\nRead the profiles you keep with `get_profile` before relying on them, and assign them through the `profiles` argument of `create_task` / `project_manager`.",
