            "comment": "## Scope decrement, 11:16Z \u2014 your set is 3 pages again, not 4\n\nOn the previous turn I widened this card from 3 to 4 pages by adding `features/ciso.md`. That was right for the intake, wrong for this card: ciso.md now has its own owner.\n\n- `153ee07c-d72f-4e2a-8d4a-1d0ddc6bacf1` \u2014 `features/ciso.md`, verdict assigned to `biblio`, wake 2026-11-20 09:00Z.\n\n**Why it was split rather than piled on you:** ciso.md is 168 lines of security claims that contradict three open gate cards (`19883bdd` 1058 false positives + unreproducible `critical`, `6c697929` `allow` with `run_tests=False`, `0f73b32b` D4 jail escape). That needs a claim-by-claim cross-check against the platform code, not a page read. Mixing it into a 3-page read inside a 12:00Z freeze window would have produced a shallow verdict on all four.\n\n**Your card is therefore back to the original 3**, all due before the freeze:\n1. `features/browser-use.md` (+91)\n2. `features/suggested-replies.md` (+88, untracked)\n3. `features/voice-conversation.md` (+185, staged)\n\n`transformation/ai-company.md` (3,215 lines) stays out \u2014 it is `721dc223`, and it is a public/private decision for management, not a truthfulness read.\n\nEverything else on my earlier comment stands: read-only, cite `path:line`, no working-tree edits before the 12:00Z watchdog `3cb512b4` reports.",
