            "comment": "## Intake closed, 11:16Z \u2014 all 5 unowned pages now have an owner\n\nThis card's job was to make sure nothing unpublished reaches the build without a name against it. That job is done; recording the final mapping so the card can be closed rather than re-run.\n\n| File | Lines | State | Owner card |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `features/voice-conversation.md` | +185 | staged `A` | `68566d25` (truth read) |\n| `features/suggested-replies.md` | +88 | staged `A` | `68566d25` (truth read) |\n| `features/browser-use.md` | +91 | staged `M` | `68566d25` (truth read) |\n| `features/ciso.md` | 168 | **untracked** | **`153ee07c` \u2014 created 11:16Z, owner `biblio`** |\n| `transformation/ai-company.md` | 3,215 | **untracked** | `721dc223` (public/private decision) |\n\nThe fifth entry is the gap this card was hiding: ciso.md was untracked, 168 lines, and already wired into the nav (`config.mts`), the catalogue (`features/index.md`) and `users-and-security.md`. No card on the board owned it. Verified by query before creating: `list_tasks(query=\"features/ciso.md\")` \u2192 0 results on a 23-card board.\n\n**Also worth carrying forward, since it is not a page problem:** `.vitepress/config.mts` has no `srcExclude`. Every `.md` under the docs root compiles, whether tracked, staged or untracked. So \"approve the 7 staged files\" and \"approve what the next build publishes\" are different sets \u2014 7 vs 10. That distinction is now on `a8be6182` and `3cb512b4`.\n\nNothing further needed here unless a sixth unowned file appears. Recommend closing this card at the next checkpoint rather than waiting for 21 Nov \u2014 its deliverable (a complete, owned mapping) has shipped.",
            "chat_id": "2410a44c-186f-4bb6-ae86-49880c71d484"
          },
          "response": "{\n  \"status\": \"comment_added\",\n  \"task_id\": \"2410a44c-186f-4bb6-ae86-49880c71d484\",\n  \"message_id\": null,\n  \"processed\": false\n}",
          "output": "\ud83d\udcdd Comment added to task **Intake \u2014 four unowned files sit in the working tree management approves tomorrow (voice-conversation docs page + attribution spec + 2 nav lines)**.\n- ID: `2410a44c-186f-4bb6-ae86-49880c71d484`\n- No processing was triggered: the request waits for a user.",
